                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the model & unit economics`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `You have the P&L, the CAC/LTV data and the pilot results. Blended CAC is <strong>€34</strong> against an LTV of <strong>€41</strong> — a <strong>1.2x</strong> ratio, far below the <strong>3.0x</strong> investors expect. Diagnose <em>why the consumer model burns cash</em>: each user costs more than it returns, and growth at these economics burns money faster, not slower. Then find where Venturely's <strong>sustainable value</strong> — verified emissions cuts and city outcomes — is currently given away free while you pay to acquire consumers. Cities pay for outcomes; that is the unpriced revenue hiding in your model.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Design the digital-sustainable model`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Choose what kind of business Venturely is. <strong>A) Consumer app</strong> — big TAM, weak economics and moat. <strong>B) B2B city SaaS/data</strong> — sell verified emissions cuts and mobility insights to municipalities: smaller TAM, strong margins and retention, slower sales. <strong>C) Ecosystem/platform</strong> — others build on your APIs: network effects but needs scale. With €6M and 24 months you can build <em>one</em> well. Reset the revenue mechanic so <strong>digital and sustainable value compound</strong> — sustainability becomes priced revenue, not cost — and drive the unit economics toward ≥3.0x.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Decide how to deploy generative AI`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Generative AI sits unused on the table. A full LLM deployment costs <strong>~€45K/month</strong> — about 20% of your €220K burn. Deployed on the wrong job it is a runway leak; deployed on the right one it lifts gross margin and wins B2B deals. The strongest fit is <strong>automating municipal emissions reporting and analytics — a task cities actually pay for</strong>. Decide the use-case, <em>build vs. buy</em>, and the monthly budget. AI must be a value driver, not a slogan: which single use-case earns its €45K?`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Position in the ecosystem & pitch the raise`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `A global mobility super-app is entering Iberia and courting the same cities and charging networks. You have a <strong>two-quarter window</strong> to lock a defensible position before it disintermediates you — putting the €6M raise and €1.4M ARR at risk. Choose: <strong>data/insights partner to cities</strong>, <strong>integration hub</strong> for operators, or <strong>consumer aggregator</strong>. Name the wedge that reaches scale before the giant does. Then pitch the €6M Series A — and make the model, the AI plan and the position <em>one coherent story</em>, because an investor pulls the first loose thread.`,

                    r1_diagnosis_label:     `Why does the current consumer-app model burn cash?`,
                    r1_unpriced_label:      `Where is sustainable value currently given away rather than monetised?`,
                    r1_target_label:        `Set the LTV/CAC target you will commit to investors (x)`,
                    r1_target_readout:      `Committed LTV/CAC target:`,
                    r1_target_x:            `x`,
                    r1_target_hint:         `Investors expect ≥ 3.0x. Promising 1.2x signals you accept a broken model; promising 5.0x with no mechanism signals you do not understand it.`,
                    diag_economics:         `Broken unit economics with a weak moat — CAC €34 beats a defensible LTV €41, so every new user loses money and growth burns faster`,
                    diag_marketing:         `We just under-market — more paid acquisition and a louder brand would fix the numbers`,
                    diag_product:           `The app needs more features — once retention rises the economics sort themselves out`,
                    diag_runway:            `Nothing structural — we only need the €6M; the model is fine, we are simply early`,
                    unpriced_cities:        `Verified emissions cuts and mobility outcomes — cities pay for those, yet we hand them over free while paying to acquire consumers`,
                    unpriced_brand:         `Nowhere — sustainability is a brand halo, not something anyone would pay for`,
                    unpriced_consumers:     `From consumers — we should charge users a green premium for the eco-routing feature`,
                    unpriced_none:          `It is not given away — we already capture all the value we create`,

                    r2_model_label:         `Choose the business model to build with the €6M.`,
                    r2_pricing_label:       `Reset the revenue mechanic — how do you price sustainable value?`,
                    r2_invest_label:        `Where do you concentrate the €6M? (share to the chosen model's go-to-market, %)`,
                    r2_invest_readout:      `Capital concentrated on the chosen model:`,
                    r2_pct:                 `%`,
                    r2_invest_hint:         `With €6M and 24 months you can build one model well. Spreading the capital thin across all three signals strategic confusion and reaches scale in none.`,
                    model_consumer:         `A — Consumer app: chase the big TAM, scale users fast, fix economics later`,
                    model_saas:             `B — B2B city SaaS/data: sell verified emissions cuts & mobility insights to municipalities; strong margins, slower sales`,
                    model_platform:         `C — Ecosystem/platform: open APIs so transit & charging operators build on you; network effects, needs scale`,
                    model_everything:       `All three at once — keep the consumer app, sell to cities, and open the platform; decide later`,
                    pricing_outcomes:       `Price the outcome — sell cities verified emissions reductions, reporting and mobility insights as paid products`,
                    pricing_freemium:       `Freemium consumer upsell — keep the app free, charge a small premium for eco features`,
                    pricing_ads:            `Ad-funded — keep everything free and monetise attention; sustainability stays a marketing line`,
                    pricing_unchanged:      `Leave pricing unchanged — push volume and revisit monetisation after the raise`,

                    r3_usecase_label:       `Where do you deploy generative AI against its ~€45K/month cost?`,
                    r3_buildbuy_label:      `Build vs. buy the AI capability.`,
                    r3_spend_label:         `Monthly generative-AI budget you commit (€K/month)`,
                    r3_spend_readout:       `GenAI spend:`,
                    r3_spend_unit:          `K€/mo`,
                    r3_spend_hint:          `Full deployment is ~€45K/month — 20% of your €220K burn. On the right single use-case it earns its keep; spread across unmonetised features it is a pure runway leak.`,
                    usecase_ops:            `Operations — automate municipal emissions reporting & analytics, a task cities pay for (lifts margin, wins B2B deals)`,
                    usecase_consumer:       `Consumer — AI trip-planning and personalised nudges (boosts engagement, hard to monetise)`,
                    usecase_everywhere:     `Everywhere — put an LLM in the app, the city dashboard and the help desk because investors expect AI`,
                    usecase_notnow:         `Not now — defer AI entirely and protect the runway`,
                    buildbuy_buy:           `Buy — start on a foundation-model API; cheap, fast, validate ROI before committing`,
                    buildbuy_finetune:      `Fine-tune — adapt a model on your municipal data once the use-case is proven (defensible, moderate cost)`,
                    buildbuy_inhouse:       `Build in-house — train your own model now for maximum control (slow, burns scarce runway)`,

                    r4_position_label:      `Choose Venturely's ecosystem position.`,
                    r4_wedge_label:         `What is your wedge to reach scale before the super-app does?`,
                    r4_coherence_label:     `How tightly do model, AI plan and ecosystem position tell ONE story to investors? (%)`,
                    r4_coherence_hint:      `An investor pulls the first loose thread. If the model says B2B, the AI serves consumers and the position is aggregator, the pitch unravels. Make the three one story.`,
                    position_data:          `Preferred data/insights partner to cities — own the municipal relationship and the outcome reporting`,
                    position_hub:           `Integration hub for transit & charging operators — be the layer everyone connects through`,
                    position_aggregator:    `Consumer aggregator — compete head-on with the super-app for the citizen's home screen`,
                    wedge_pilot:            `Turn the live pilot city into a lighthouse reference, then land neighbouring municipalities on its proof`,
                    wedge_discount:         `Undercut the super-app on price and out-spend it on consumer acquisition`,
                    wedge_wait:             `Stay broad and wait — keep all options open until the market picks a winner`,

                    warn_target_range:      `The LTV/CAC target must be between 1.0x and 5.0x.`,
                    warn_invest_range:      `Capital concentration must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
