                    insight_fundable:       `Series A fundable: you solved it as one system — a focused B2B city model that prices sustainable value to ≥3.0x economics, AI on the reporting cities pay for, and a defensible data-partner position the super-app can't simply take. The model, the AI plan and the ecosystem position tell one story an investor can pull on.`,
                    insight_aileak:         `Runway burned on AI: you deployed generative AI across use-cases that don't monetise — ~20% of your burn for engagement and show. The cheapest way to lose a 9-month runway is to spend a fifth of it proving you can put an LLM everywhere.`,
                    insight_incoherent:     `Incoherent raise: the model, the AI plan and the ecosystem position pointed in different directions, and the first thread an investor pulled unravelled the pitch. A startup that signals it doesn't know what it is doesn't close a Series A.`,
                    insight_short:          `You didn't fully reconcile the four decisions. The economics, the model, the AI plan and the position still tell slightly different stories — enough for an investor to find the seam and the super-app to find the opening.`,
                    insight_economics_fixed: `Unit economics fixed: you reached ≥3.0x LTV/CAC by pricing sustainable value to the customer who pays for outcomes — the city — rather than chasing consumer growth on a broken 1.2x model. That is the line between scaling and burning.`,
                    insight_economics_broken: `Unit economics stayed broken: at well under 3.0x, growth still burns money faster than it makes it. Until pricing and the customer change, the €6M only postpones the same runway cliff.`,
                    insight_runway_low:     `Runway is dangerously low: cash discipline slipped — likely an over-funded acquisition push, AI for show, or a price war with the super-app. The Series A had to close by month 6, and you cut it fine.`,
                    insight_moat_strong:    `Strong ecosystem moat: you locked a defensible position — the city data relationship and verified outcomes — before the super-app could disintermediate you. That is what protects the €6M raise and the €1.4M ARR.`,
                    insight_model_focus:    `Strategic focus paid off: by choosing the B2B city model and concentrating the €6M on it, you built one thing well instead of three things half-way — the discipline investors fund.`,

                    hint_ai:                `Your generative-AI spend is leaking runway on use-cases that don't monetise. Concentrate it on automating the municipal reporting cities actually pay for, or pull it back to protect the cash.`,
                    hint_runway:            `Runway is critically low. Stop the bleed — an over-funded consumer push, AI for show or a price war all burn the cash the Series A is meant to replace. Protect the months to close.`,
                    hint_economics:         `Your LTV/CAC is still far below 3.0x. Growth won't save a broken model — change who pays and how you price sustainable value, not how much you acquire.`,
                    hint_coherence:         `Your decisions don't tell one story yet. Align the model, the AI plan and the ecosystem position into a single defensible thread before the pitch.`,
                    hint_moat:              `Your ecosystem moat is thin with the super-app circling. Anchor a defensible position — the city data relationship and verified outcomes — and a wedge that reaches scale first.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — 3.0x economics, investor confidence and a real moat. Lock the coherent story: model, AI plan and ecosystem position pointing the same way into the pitch.`,

